    proxy-assigned identity to key on, since before that a caller could reset its own quota by
    changing its own <code>Authorization</code> header. <b>Unlike v0.0.1, this release was tagged
    without running its live-provider drill</b> — it exists
    (<code>testing/diffrig/tests/live_gate_v0_1_0.rs</code>, one command, three billable calls) and
    was deliberately not run before tagging; recorded in <code>internal-docs/MILESTONES.md</code> as a named
    departure, not a gap that was missed. WP-35's scope closed narrower than its title:
    same-dialect fallback only — cross-dialect (openai → anthropic) is a deliberate hard error,
    split into new WP-52 (v1.0.0) rather than left as a silent gap.</span>
    <span class="gate"><b>v0.2.0's SHIP GATE — CLOSED, shipped 2026-08-29 (tag <code>v0.2.0</code>).</b>
    A published capacity report (p99, tokens/sec ceiling, RSS under sustained long-lived streams)
    from a run that is not harness-bound, plus <code>/config_dump</code> and <code>/stats</code>
    on the admin endpoint, plus a config swap under live traffic with zero dropped streams. All
    three met: <code>/config_dump</code>/<code>/stats</code> closed 2026-08-09
    (<code>/stats</code> reports real traffic, not an empty registry —
    <code>crates/proxy/tests/stats_e2e.rs</code>); the swap clause closed the same day
    (<code>testing/diffrig/tests/swap_under_load.rs</code>, terminal-frame assertion, not a
    request count); the capacity report published <code>054b809</code> after two loadgen
