    <code>0d7bd1b</code>; HTTP upgrades/WebSocket tunneling (WP-10 S10) landed the same window as
    a bonus, not gate-required. Full history of this gate's long path to closing is in
    <code>internal-docs/MILESTONES.md</code>, not repeated here now that it's shipped.</span>
    <span class="gate"><b>v0.3.2's SHIP GATE (carried over from v0.3.0, which was tagged without it) — still RED.</b> The proxy
    takes its entire configuration from an ADS control plane, ACKs and NACKs correctly per S8,
    and survives a control-plane reconnect with make-before-break cluster warming. <b>WP-20 (ADS
    client) is DONE, 2026-09-05/06 — all six increments.</b> It opens a real gRPC stream,
    ACKs/NACKs, reconnects and resyncs forever with a jittered backoff, applies accepted LDS/CDS
    resources into the IR, all five WP-28 acceptance scenarios pass over a real socket, and
    <code>make xds-conformance</code> found and fixed a real deadlock against a pinned
    go-control-plane on its first run — evidence for why that opt-in target exists, since our own
