    visible but still open by design</b>: a 20-token/minute budget survived six ~16-token
    requests with zero 429s because the limiter read no usage and said nothing; now warns loudly
    (at most once per budget key per minute) but still admits the request uncharged — an owner
    decision, not a partial fix. Root cause is architectural: <code>body_rewrite</code>'s
    anti-spoofing rewrite can re-route a request onto a route whose usage dialect no longer
    matches the response shape, and WP-35's card now
    carries the prerequisite this forces — the usage dialect must move from the route to the
    cluster before WP-52 makes cross-dialect fallback legal, see WP-34/WP-35/WP-52's cards.
    Re-run directly this refresh: 4 of 7 <code>local_openai_smoke.rs</code> cases pass, 3
